{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And you shall observe the matzot, etc.</b> Meaning: just as I observed the day and did not delay even one day, and on the very essence of this day I brought you out — for this reason you too shall not delay the matzah until it leavens." "It further says <b>and you shall observe this day</b> — the El likewise commands that a person must also safeguard the day itself, so as not to err in the reckoning, neither advancing nor delaying the observance of this day and no other day in its place. And this entire interpretation is stated under <b>ki be'etzem</b> (for in the very essence), which illuminates both right and left: it illuminates to give a reason for what precedes it — the observing of the matzot — and it illuminates what follows it — the observing of the day — in this manner: כִּי בְּעֶצֶם (for in the very essence) etc., meaning, for the reason that בְּעֶצֶם הַיּוֹם (on the very essence of the day) etc., [therefore] וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם (you too shall observe) this day as well."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:06.605041464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}